{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "07Y3", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{proposition-second-diagonal-representable}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:860fdf81879d64c758e9b613b221a3a83a67f7ac9ff01b655aa89d8066e1878c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nProposition <REF_0001> is our first\nmain result on algebraic stacks.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:29a616e0405e9d5bf08194dc6e34491b02a9e4cfe6a4a720dffc0e71e35b17f3", "unit_id": "tag:07Y3:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "07Y3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$p : \\mathcal{X} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Delta : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_{S, s}$", "MATH_0008": "$s$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-axioms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-diagonal-representable}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:51bbe5026506482dd23386a14ebcd8b65882a8c7b3154529849993cc2da1b522", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:970c7d3ac38cb74c29954a165d8ba7d308233383ce3304dcbc75ed31b2152822", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let\n<MATH_0002> be a category fibred in groupoids.\nAssume that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003>\nis representable by algebraic spaces,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0004> satisfies axioms [-1], [0], [1], [2], [3] (see\nSection <REF_0001>),\n<STRUCT_0004> every formal object of <MATH_0005> is effective,\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0006> satisfies openness of versality, and\n<STRUCT_0006> <MATH_0007> is a G-ring for all finite type points <MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009>.\n<STRUCT_0007>\nThen <MATH_0010> is an algebraic stack.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:65e17a910d41da8e189e373f0b806284c3436220a8fb69b03b52f8926cd0c461", "unit_id": "tag:07Y4:statement"}
